{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues","id":1256534,"title":"The Ravnos; Paradoxical Rogues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-22T13:41:49-07:00","id":1256534,"title":"The Ravnos; Paradoxical Rogues","content":"Note: This is a preamble. If you just want to see the writeup, which I'm doing in the style of a V20 Clan writeup, then you can skip to the next post :-)<br /> <br /> So I've done this before, and I've gone about it the wrong way. I decided to read V20's presentation of the Ravnos, carefully, and figure out exactly what it is about it that means I don't use it at my table. To fix something you need to understand what's wrong with it.<br /> <br /> Ravnos are characterised as rogues, tricksters and outsiders. Hated and despised by the other clans. Seemingly more so than the Setites and Caitiff, indeed! It's strongly implied that they do lots of stuff to piss off the powers that be, but the V20 writeup doesn't devote that much space to explaining what that is; the implication is that it's theft.<br /> <br /> - Tricksters<br /> - Thieves<br /> - Rogues<br /> - Despised Outsiders<br /> - Strong links with the Romani<br /> - Nomadic<br /> <br /> On its own, this is kind of lackluster, and really superfluous. Caitiff are your scapegoats. Gangrel are your nomadic outsiders, carrying tales with them. And &quot;trickster&quot; isn't a Clan concept, it's a Path concept really. A clan of tricksters isn't a functional concept.<br /> <br /> So my idea was to reform their lore somewhat. Starting with Vampiric society, you have the Traditions. And in most Domains in the Kindred world, those matter a lot. So rather than having them be &quot;thieves&quot;, let's have them be a clan which never really got on board with the Traditions. The smallest of the 13 clans, their behaviour has been shaped by their Methuselahs and Elders. The least organized, but paradoxically the most united.<br /> <br /> My goal is to revise the Ravnos to be:<br /> <br /> - &quot;Thieves&quot; and outlaws by the standards of Kindred, rather than by the standards of humans<br /> - Outsiders in a different sense to the Gangrel; they're not nomadic and animalistic, they're decidedly nomadic in a human way<br /> - Place more emphasis on links with &quot;travelers&quot; of all kinds than with the Romani in particular<br /> <br /> I'm trying to do this in a way which works with the existing concepts and lore, rather than completely revising them or just tacking on random new stuff like &quot;they're basically the Camarilla in India&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T13:48:07-07:00","id":1256537,"title":"","content":"I think the treatment in Ravnos Revised more or less eliminates any need to &quot;fix&quot; the Ravnos. The best part of that book is that it fixed not only the Ravnos but multiple other problems with the bloodline as a whole.<br /> <br /> 1. The over-reliance on Western vampirism myths. By adding Rakshasa to the Kindred mythology, they have expanded to include one of the most prevalent monsters in Indian mythology with a rich cultural history.<br /> <br /> 2. The expanding of the Ravnos beyond &quot;gypsy&quot; stereotypes and instead incorporating the entirety of Indian mythology and one of the largest ethnic groups in the world getting their own clan. The fact Romani are Europeans of Indian descent also means the ludicrous stereotype neatly slides into their role as an effect of Kindred racism.<br /> <br /> 3. The fact corruption, vice, temptation, and frigging illusion is all stuff which Rakshasa are known for in mythology.<br /> <br /> 4. Highlighting that Ravnos culture is actually extremely traditionalist, classicist, and brutal with the people we meet tending to be the Outcasts (literally) of their race.<br /> <br /> Suddenly their Discipline has a historical basis as does their Clan flaw.<br /> <br /> So, yes, it was, to me at least, as simple as making them the &quot;Indian&quot; vampires versus the Romani vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T14:00:07-07:00","id":1256538,"title":"","content":"The Ravnos are the smallest of the clans, and they move through the night with a freedom other Kindred can't begin to understand. Forget the Traditions. Forget Clan Hierarchy. Forget Primogeniture, Princes, Bishops, Elders... the Ravnos try to move past all of it. &quot;Anarchs&quot; in the most literal and puerile sense, they reject most of the basic foundations of Kindred society. They &quot;poach&quot; by feeding in the domains of others, they skip town with the item the whole court was fighting over, they disrespect the authority of Sect and society. To the Ravnos, these things are profane, and they take joy in disregarding them.<br /> <br /> In a society as structured and paranoid as that of most Kindred, this simply is not acceptable. The Ravnos are not polite outsiders who behave and follow the rules to avoid pissing off the local rulers. Here they may be distinguished from the Gangrel, and other Independent Clans and Bloodlines. They aren't even Rebels; they're Rogues. The Camarilla despises the Ravnos as a result, and has levied many resources towards maligning and scandalizing them, building on truth and lie to warp their reputation. Some Kindred historians believe that this has even shaped human history; the Ravnos are human-like nomads, and they travel with Travelers for protection, blood and companionship. So 1000s of years of propaganda from Princes may have warped the way kine perceive these traveler communities; when Roma were thrown out of villages with bloodied noses, perhaps once Kindred were pulling their strings.<br /> <br /> The simplest way to explain the Ravnos's place in Kindred society is to talk about the sort of effect they have on a Domain. There's an order to things. In-fighting, politicking, backstabbing, they're all ongoing. Everyone has a few skeletons in their closet, and the city is abuzz over one issue or another. By the time the so-called Deceiver has left town a lot of strands in this delicate web have been torn and tangled. Old alliances are bent out of shape, and Kindred find themselves with strange bedfellows. It is the Ravnos's self-appointed duty to shake things up and undo the stasis of Kindred society.<br /> <br /> For the Ravnos, the greatest values are those of community and independence. This seems paradoxical to some, but the clan is full of contradictions. They disregard the Masquerade in theory, and yet for the most part they keep it. For them it tends to be a personal matter of privacy rather than some grand intoxicating secret. Their human companions tend to know who and what they are, and they are not always ghouls.<br /> <br /> While a Ravnos is staying within a Domain, they tend to hunt however they wish, and use this as a chance to stake out the local Kindred society. &quot;Mischief&quot; is an oversimplified way of putting it, but many do seek to throw a spanner in the works. What can they do that would cause the most disruption to this ordered fascist shit-show?<br /> <br /> Some among the Ravnos follow the Path of Paradox, which codifies the Clan's culture and beliefs as a system of morality. These mystics hold their own secrets, and practice rare forms of blood magic.<br /> <br /> Clan Ravnos is well known for its signature Discipline of Chimerstry; using it they can create illusions and warp perceptions, and with its greatest powers they begin to warp reality itself.<br /> <br /> Nickname: Deceivers<br /> <br /> Sect: The Ravnos, as a general rule, are Independent. There are few exceptions due to their reputation, and the concerted efforts of Elder Ravnos and Elders within the Camarilla and Sabbat. Some Ravnos ally themselves with the Anarchs, albeit in an informal manner.<br /> <br /> Appearance: Ravnos tend to embrace out of traveling communities, such as the Romani and Irish Travelers. However those who choose nomadic lifestyles and give up on structured society may be an enticing prospect to a Ravnos; as a result they may hail from any background. Many of the Elders of the clan have Egyptian, Eastern European and even Indian heritage.<br /> <br /> Haven: Most Ravnos live on the road. Caravans, RVs, motels, trailer parks... if a Ravnos is staying within a Domain for a few weeks or months they may set down some roots and find themselves nice accommodation, but their home is rarely truly fixed.<br /> <br /> Background: Ravnos tend to embrace self-sufficient people who exist on the edges of society, especially people who find society absurd or defy it in some way. Punks, bikers, travelers, the homeless, refugees and immigrants; the Ravnos prefer to embrace those who need no lesson in what is wrong with ordered societies like the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Character Creation: Indepedent concepts are common. Ravnos have diverse and fluid backgrounds, rather than being fortified in one place. Some allies here and there, some money in international accounts. Physical and Social attributes are often primary, and Talents and Skills are often predominant.<br /> <br /> Clan Disciplines: Chimerstry, Presence and Fortitude<br /> <br /> Weaknesses: The Ravnos are impulsive, having a kind of rebellious individualism in their very blood. Every Ravnos has some kind of &quot;virtue&quot; or &quot;vice&quot; which can manifest as compulsive behaviour. Ravnos must roll Self-Control, difficulty 6, to avoid sating their impulse when tempted by an opportunity. Those on Paths which use Instinct separate themselves from the restraints which hold them back from impulse, and therefore do not roll to resist the temptation towards virtue or vice. Examples include an urge to punish abusive people, urges to help defenseless young people, urges to scam others or urges to inflict emotional pain.<br /> <br /> Organization: The clan is fragmented yet strangely united. Some postulate that the power of their Methuselahs (or even their Antedeluvian!) is felt through the blood via the power of Presence, leading to a relatively cohesive clan philosophy. Others simply point out that the Ravnos are left in a position where their only choice is to go with the grain and follow the clan's culture of chaotic and paradoxical rebellion. The opinions of the Sects and the other Clans don't leave room for them to avoid this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-22-2018, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T14:02:18-07:00","id":1256539,"title":"","content":"Good write-up!<br /> <br /> I like it, and the use of paradoxical.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T14:04:17-07:00","id":1256541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues#post1256534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: This is a preamble. If you just want to see the writeup, which I'm doing in the style of a V20 Clan writeup, then you can skip to the next post :-)<br /> <br /> So I've done this before, and I've gone about it the wrong way. I decided to read V20's presentation of the Ravnos, carefully, and figure out exactly what it is about it that means I don't use it at my table. To fix something you need to understand what's wrong with it.<br /> <br /> Ravnos are characterised as rogues, tricksters and outsiders. Hated and despised by the other clans. Seemingly more so than the Setites and Caitiff, indeed! It's strongly implied that they do lots of stuff to piss off the powers that be, but the V20 writeup doesn't devote that much space to explaining what that is; the implication is that it's theft.<br /> <br /> - Tricksters<br /> - Thieves<br /> - Rogues<br /> - Despised Outsiders<br /> - Strong links with the Romani<br /> - Nomadic<br /> <br /> On its own, this is kind of lackluster, and really superfluous. Caitiff are your scapegoats. Gangrel are your nomadic outsiders, carrying tales with them. And &quot;trickster&quot; isn't a Clan concept, it's a Path concept really. A clan of tricksters isn't a functional concept.<br /> <br /> So my idea was to reform their lore somewhat. Starting with Vampiric society, you have the Traditions. And in most Domains in the Kindred world, those matter a lot. So rather than having them be &quot;thieves&quot;, let's have them be a clan which never really got on board with the Traditions. The smallest of the 13 clans, their behaviour has been shaped by their Methuselahs and Elders. The least organized, but paradoxically the most united.<br /> <br /> My goal is to revise the Ravnos to be:<br /> <br /> - &quot;Thieves&quot; and outlaws by the standards of Kindred, rather than by the standards of humans<br /> - Outsiders in a different sense to the Gangrel; they're not nomadic and animalistic, they're decidedly nomadic in a human way<br /> - Place more emphasis on links with &quot;travelers&quot; of all kinds than with the Romani in particular<br /> <br /> I'm trying to do this in a way which works with the existing concepts and lore, rather than completely revising them or just tacking on random new stuff like &quot;they're basically the Camarilla in India&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a noble aim. I'd point out that &quot;Travellers&quot; is also a common name for Roma around Europe too, so maybe &quot;Wanderers&quot; would be a better description. And, honestly, I think it would be best if all direct cultural ties to Romani should be removed. It was actually the case that the Gangrel were descibed as the 'gypsie' Clan back in the first couple of editions, and were then removed. With the Ravnos, if it were to be introduced as a relatively minor Clan and based on an archetype of the criminal class in human society, generally, then this could be workable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T14:07:01-07:00","id":1256543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1256541#post1256541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a noble aim. I'd point out that &quot;Travellers&quot; is also a common name for Roma around Europe too, so maybe &quot;Wanderers&quot; would be a better description. And, honestly, I think it would be best if all direct cultural ties to Romani should be removed. It was actually the case that the Gangrel were descibed as the 'gypsie' Clan back in the first couple of editions, and were then removed. With the Ravnos, if it were to be introduced as a relatively minor Clan and based on an archetype of the criminal class in human society, generally, then this could be workable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there an issue with them being the Indian clan?<br /> <br /> At least in terms of being guys who derive from their myths?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T14:22:11-07:00","id":1256548,"title":"","content":"I really like it and I did something similar , my Ravnos are an fragmented clan maybe a bloodline.They only have few elders like hazimel who is said to be dead (Fake) and all of this comes from the fact that they did succed in their anarch revolution wich is a reason for the camarilla to fear and despise them , while the anarch try to make them part of the movement but they have failed becuase the clan is very individualistic and you cannot convince the ravnos as a group.<br /> <br /> Now the clan is fragmented in two factions the traditional one and the anarch one both are indepent.The traditional one only wants to keep their domains in India and stop the Kue Jin menace becuase they are their ancestral enemies and mission.The anarch one only wants to be left alone , they won freedom from their sires long ago and they embraced very freely making the great part of the clan only know the basic about the clan.They are boundless but also unprotected so they are easy to discriminate even more if you don\u00b4t have caitiff.<br /> <br /> It\u00b4s clan weakness is also reworked they loss dicepool equal to their bane severity if they don\u00b4t commit their crime every night so even the high willpower ravnos are seen as criminals becuase they need it to be fully funtional.That gives them a lot of problems and it\u00b4s the reason for them to be travelers criminals aren\u00b4t well recived , less when they are unbound.They know that they are not well recibed so they have no reason to nice.They are criminals , thiefs and paradoxical tricksters becuase of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 09-22-2018, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T14:25:48-07:00","id":1256549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1256543#post1256543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there an issue with them being the Indian clan?<br /> <br /> At least in terms of being guys who derive from their myths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'd like to see all these extra Clans trying to be reimagined in more 'social class' terms rather than geographical/ethnic groups. Having them being the 'Indian Clan' is somewhat less offensive than calling them the 'Romani Clan' insofar that the stereotype presented of tricksters and thieves is a common, negative prejudice that Roma have to deal with all the time. It's these stereotypings that had them targetted for genocide - so that is why it is very troubling. The 'Indian stereotype' I'm not so sure, but it would be nice to create a wandering Clan without needing to make suggestions about any particular real world ethnicity. Social stereotypes are better because they are reflecting on our own society, rather than the 'other'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T16:08:13-07:00","id":1256570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1256549#post1256549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I'd like to see all these extra Clans trying to be reimagined in more 'social class' terms rather than geographical/ethnic groups. Having them being the 'Indian Clan' is somewhat less offensive than calling them the 'Romani Clan' insofar that the stereotype presented of tricksters and thieves is a common, negative prejudice that Roma have to deal with all the time. It's these stereotypings that had them targetted for genocide - so that is why it is very troubling. The 'Indian stereotype' I'm not so sure, but it would be nice to create a wandering Clan without needing to make suggestions about any particular real world ethnicity. Social stereotypes are better because they are reflecting on our own society, rather than the 'other'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I normally agree but I also think India is such a rich overlooked environment that it's good to put Cainites there.<br /> <br /> Especially as I'm really not fond of the Kindred of the East.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T16:23:56-07:00","id":1256572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1256570#post1256570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I normally agree but I also think India is such a rich overlooked environment that it's good to put Cainites there.<br /> <br /> Especially as I'm really not fond of the Kindred of the East.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but couldn't the context of the vampiric Clans themselves, move away from geographical specifications entirely? difficult to do with canon as it has been written over the years, I know, but really is it not possible to have the subcontinent have it's own flavour of Ventrue, Brujah and Nosferatu, and so on, also?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 09-22-2018, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T16:26:46-07:00","id":1256573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1256572#post1256572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but couldn;t the context of the vampiric Clans themselves, move away from geographical specifications entirely? difficult to do with canon as it has been written over the years, I know, but really is it not possible to have the subcontinent have it's own flavour of Ventrue, Brujah and Nosferatu, and so on, also?</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, making Ravnos a big deal in the region versus the Thieves and Conman of everywhere isn't a bad idea either.<br /> <br /> Every place can have its flavor of Tzimisce but the ones in the Carpethians are their own big deal.<br /> <br /> So, the Ravnos in India are the biggest deal because even though there are Ventrue and Lasombra, they are the dominant clan in the region because the ones in Revised are based on Indian Mythology and fit the Rakshasa legend best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T16:50:56-07:00","id":1256580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1256573#post1256573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While true, making Ravnos a big deal in the region versus the Thieves and Conman of everywhere isn't a bad idea either.<br /> <br /> Every place can have its flavor of Tzimisce but the ones in the Carpethians are their own big deal.<br /> <br /> So, the Ravnos in India are the biggest deal because even though there are Ventrue and Lasombra, they are the dominant clan in the region because the ones in Revised are based on Indian Mythology and fit the Rakshasa legend best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different regions may have different political dynamics, in the same way different cities do - but when you make it 'the Indian Clan' it feels like 1 billion + people are being stereotyped. The Clans are stereotypes, of course, but the less they are directly tied to specific locations the better they will be. So you could say the Ravnos are the dominant Clan is region X, but don't write it as though they are a representation of the culture, geography or ethnicity of region X. Indeed, have it so that a Ravnos coming from Region Y may well be different to that coming from Region X <i>because </i>of the cultural differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 09-22-2018, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T17:03:40-07:00","id":1256581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1256580#post1256580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Different regions may have different political dynamics, in the same way different cities do - but when you make it 'the Indian Clan' it feels like 1 billion + people are being stereotyped. The Clans are stereotypes, of course, but the less they are directly tied to specific locations the better they will be. So you could say the Ravnos are the dominant Clan is region X, but don't write it as though they are a representation of the culture, geography or ethnicity of region X. Indeed, have it so that a Ravnos coming from Region Y may well be different to that coming from Region X <i>because </i>of the cultural differences.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but I suppose it's like you also need more than the stereotype to be a good clan.<br /> <br /> The Brujah are not just the angry bikers, they also have the incredibly smart people and revolutionaries.<br /> <br /> The Toreador have the artistes but they also have the poseurs and scheming Machiavellian types.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue are the merchant class...and the old school knights.<br /> <br /> I worry a bit much the Ravnos get stuck with, &quot;wandering thieves.&quot;<br /> <br /> When the Gangrel are already the wanderers and the Malkavians are the Tricksters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T17:07:42-07:00","id":1256583,"title":"","content":"I like them having ties to the Roma in the same way that they have ties to traveling biker gangs and Irish Travelers and other minorities, and sub-cultures which travel like circuses and fairs. There's nothing wrong with the Ravnos having some ties to the Roma, as long as they don't become the &quot;Roma Clan&quot; again.<br /> <br /> p.s. I finished my core writeup. I might edit it more but that's the bare bones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T17:38:38-07:00","id":1256588,"title":"","content":"STEREOTYPES:<br /> <br /> Assamite: &quot;The Camarilla don't trust us, because we've never lied to them. We're there to fuck things up, and we're clear about that when all is said and done. These guys get some trust though, which tells you everything you need to know.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I hate a moving target...&quot;<br /> <br /> Brujah: &quot;If you're looking for a simple way to stir up trouble, there are some painfully obvious places to start. Good tools, though some I would call brother.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;They're headed in the right direction, but you'd be a fool to trust one.&quot;<br /> <br /> Followers of Set: &quot;They've got dirt on everyone. Play the part of the easily indoctrinated outsider, and see what you can pick up.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;They present a wonderful opportunity. Scapegoats are so much fun, and they won't be around to complain.&quot;<br /> <br /> Gangrel: &quot;We have a distant sort of kinship. We can learn from eachother, and trade stories if nothing else.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Try not to let on if you see through their bullshit... acting like you've been duped might give you the edge if you need it. You could pick a worse companion though.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ventrue: &quot;I almost feel sorry for the bitch. In a few days time the whole court will be in an uproar, and I'll be long gone.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;When we reject them it is not discrimination; it is differentiation. They have proven themselves time and time again to be unworthy of the rights our society offers, since they embrace none of the responsibilities.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: &quot;Respectable. And they have so many stories to share...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;When they're in town my silence costs double.&quot;<br /> <br /> Malkavian: &quot;If you can sift through the bullshit and find the odd diamond, they're good company.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I can hear the sobs of tomorrow's nightmares. Or at least I think I do. When they're gone I'll be sad; it's good to have someone in on the prank.&quot;<br /> <br /> Tremere: &quot;Oh they're all team players at first glance, but there's so much you can do with some of them... find a weak one and tear the whole pyramid down&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Trickery is a poor substitute for real power. Thankfully we stand united, and are safe from the chaos they bring.&quot;<br /> <br /> Giovanni: &quot;They'll sell out anyone and anything if you offer enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I do my best to seem unhappy when they show up.&quot;<br /> <br /> Toreador: &quot;If you need everyone to know something by sunrise, tell a few of them a 'secret'.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;They make for a shocking addition to a soiree... just don't expect them to play by our rules.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lasombra: &quot;There's always something you can dig up on these guys. Some of them must buy into the bullshit, but I haven't found one yet...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Illusions mean nothing in suffocating darkness. Drown them out and tear off their arms if you know what's good for you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Tzimisce: &quot;As if the Cammies weren't sick enough...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;There's something strangely noble about what they do. If you want my advice; they value honesty, and we have plenty to offer.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Camarilla: &quot;A twisted self-parodying mess. Our paradox shall tear it apart.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A threat. To be maligned, purged and stigmatized.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Sabbat: &quot;I always thought myself contrary, then I listened to these nutjobs trying to justify their cult.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Their target is hypocrisy, corruption and lies. When the Sabbat is worthy, they shall find no weakness in us. Until then they are like another Inquisition, burning out weakness.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anarchs: &quot;My home... until things are settled. Then it's time to hit the road.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Great allies when you need them. Fondly remembered once they're gone.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-22-2018, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T17:39:33-07:00","id":1256589,"title":"","content":"Eh, I can't really take them seriously as the Roma clan because the Gangrel are the Roma clan.<br /> <br /> Mostly because Gangrel have some dignity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T18:21:49-07:00","id":1256600,"title":"","content":"What kind of western or european concepts do you think would work for the settled (Dharma focused) side of the Ravnos as represented by the majority who occupy India? I find them very intriguing and think they add a great balance to the clan. Better, it adds story and an improved mythos. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T18:42:19-07:00","id":1256605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1256581#post1256581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True but I suppose it's like you also need more than the stereotype to be a good clan.<br /> <br /> The Brujah are not just the angry bikers, they also have the incredibly smart people and revolutionaries.<br /> <br /> The Toreador have the artistes but they also have the poseurs and scheming Machiavellian types.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue are the merchant class...and the old school knights.<br /> <br /> I worry a bit much the Ravnos get stuck with, &quot;wandering thieves.&quot;<br /> <br /> When the Gangrel are already the wanderers and the Malkavians are the Tricksters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The social stereotyping of the original clans reflect human social classes:<br /> <br /> Brujah - Agitating classes (some may be educated but still associate with the undertrod lower classes).<br /> Gangrel - Outsiders, rejecting civil norms/Alternative lifestyle classes (Hippies, libertarians, etc)<br /> Malkavian - Disaffected classes (freaks, weirdos, deviants) - social rejects, basically.<br /> Nosferatu - Ugly, forgotten lower class<br /> Toreador - Chattering/arty liberal class.<br /> Tremere - Rising academic/professional classes.<br /> Ventrue - Aristocratic Upper Class/the 'Establishment'<br /> <br /> Some of them have other angles, like Tremere and their Ars Magica roots, etc - but the stereotypical aspects of them are socially based rather than geographical and ethnical. That's what I'd like to see extended into the other Clans. They can still keep their essential strengths and weaknesses, just interpret them through a different lens. So the Ravnos, for example could represent the perpetually repeating criminal class, which would make their presence a tiny minority in wider vampiric society without essentially sluring a real world ethnicity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 09-22-2018, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T18:48:12-07:00","id":1256607,"title":"","content":"Making the Ravnos just criminals seems like a step back from Revised, though. They were a priestly demon fighting caste of illusionists and tempters.<br /> <br /> Now they're just con artists and thieves?<br /> <br /> Just saying.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T19:07:38-07:00","id":1256609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1256607#post1256607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making the Ravnos just criminals seems like a step back from Revised, though. They were a priestly demon fighting caste of illusionists and tempters.<br /> <br /> Now they're just con artists and thieves?<br /> <br /> Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they can be expanded on in this way as you like - that's fine by me - I'm just literally talking in broad stereotyped terms within the model of the human social classes outlined for the original seven above. It's just these stereotypes are based on our perceptions of social groups from <i>within</i> our own human society, rather than <i>outsider </i>ethnic groups, is all.<br /> <br /> Anyway, have a watch of this: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mwEi5Dpq6zs\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mwEi5Dpq6zs</a> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 09-22-2018, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T19:11:39-07:00","id":1256611,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T02:43:36-07:00","id":1256670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1256607#post1256607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making the Ravnos just criminals seems like a step back from Revised, though. They were a priestly demon fighting caste of illusionists and tempters.<br /> <br /> Now they're just con artists and thieves?<br /> <br /> Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I really want to be very clear; the Ravnos are con artists and thieves *by the standards of Kindred*. Kindred have a fucked up society that we would all be terrified of if it actually existed. The Camarilla is a proto-fascist oligarchy which practices primogeniture with immortality, corporal punishment, and gives its citizens almost no rights. So the core of the Ravnos's activity is their fundamental belief that Kindred society is rotten to the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T02:48:55-07:00","id":1256671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1256539#post1256539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good write-up!<br /> <br /> I like it, and the use of paradoxical.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Any other suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T07:09:08-07:00","id":1256704,"title":"","content":"Quote: &quot;I'm only passing through. And no, I'm not going to present myself to some Prince or Bishop... this ain't the 1300s mate.&quot;<br /> <br /> Kiasyd: &quot;They appreciate illusions, but they see through lies in an instant. Best to stay on their good side.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;When they speak my ears bleed. Why does the truth sound so strange on their tongue?&quot;<br /> <br /> Gargoyles: &quot;The free ones know what's up. Show them respect and point them towards your enemies.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The wanderer set me free. I remember her each time I strike back against my old masters.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-23-2018, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T07:21:06-07:00","id":1256707,"title":"","content":"LORE:<br /> <br /> Ravana left soon after her embrace; the rulership of the 2nd and 3rd Generation, the hierarchy, their ownership of mortals, she saw it as stagnation and injustice. Walking freely through the world she created her own tribe of wanderers. With time she embraced and fragments of this nomadic people split off, populating the world, always protected by the Ravnos who lived among them.<br /> <br /> When the flood came, she was the only one of the thirteen who was protected by loyal kine. While she was weakened by the wrath of a cruel and selfish god, the people who loved her and trusted her sacrificed much to keep her safe from the deluge.<br /> <br /> Ravana has some kind of relationship with Sutekh, and with Ennoia. It is believed that she traveled with Ennoia, the Gangrel Progenitor, for some time. They were possibly sisters (being twin daughters of Lilith according to some Bahari, both rejecting patriarchal society), or lovers, or friends. In the end they became bitter rivals according to most versions of the tale. In honour of their relationship, many Ravnos see the Gangrel as their cousins. Ravana battled with Sutekh in all versions of the tales. According to the Setites the Ravnos Progenitor was created by the Gods, along with 11 others, to fight against Set and ruin his plans. Another tale has Sutekh, the first Vampire, embracing 12 others, including Ravana as one of them. In both versions of the tale it is Ravana who brings forth chaos and betrays Set, ruining his designs and consigning him to Duat. In the Ravnos version of the tale, she tore down his temple as it was a symbol of stasis and injustice.<br /> <br /> During the Long Night, Ravnos moved through Europe without caring for the Secrecy of the Blood, so most Princes counted them among their enemies. When the Camarilla first formed, a concerted effort from several Tremere and Ventrue led to them being unofficially branded collective anathema. Of course in theory a Ravnos could be accepted into a Court, but most Princes throughout history have taken steps to destroy those who remain in their domains, or to expedite their departure. For their part, the Ravnos have no desire to join the Ivory Tower, save perhaps to gain a loftier vantage point for sabotage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T09:46:28-07:00","id":1256737,"title":"","content":"Disciplines:<br /> <br /> Chimerstry is the Ravnos's signature power. With this they manipulate the power of dreams itself, manifesting in the waking world as illusions of the external senses. Sights, smells, sounds, hot and cold, touch... this power is often the crux of a Ravnos's pranks, schemes and survival techniques.<br /> <br /> Presence allows the Ravnos to gain the trust of mortals and vampires alike, and helps them to pass as Toreador, Brujah and Ventrue when needed. Supernatural charisma can sweeten a deception and lure in support.<br /> <br /> Fortitude is an important aspect in the Ravnos's survival; in spite of the fact that they are persona non grata in the Camarilla, they continue to exist and thrive. This is because of their independence and their great survival skills for the most part, but Fortitude helps when all else fails.<br /> <br /> Antitribu:<br /> <br /> &quot;That dripping? It's water, don't worry. Blood? Guts? Kid, you must be seeing things.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Ravnos &quot;antitribu&quot; are misnamed. It is not a rejection of Clan Ravnos's ideals to join the Sabbat in the way most of these antitribu do. Ravnos in the Sabbat have aligned themselves with it as a tool to tear down the Camarilla, and to tear down the corruption within the Sabbat. Ravnos join nomadic packs and take part in Crusades, and are also a critical component of the Sabbat Inquisition, using subtlety and guile where the Ventrue use intimidation and raw strength. Some seek to reform the Sabbat, though many do fall prey to their own bestial instincts, as the Sabbat gives them many opportunities to practice their Vices, eventually losing sight of their anarchist ideals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-23-2018, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T10:51:20-07:00","id":1256752,"title":"","content":"Side-Bar: The Importance of Community<br /> <br /> Most Ravnos concepts should fall into a traveling community of some kind. A circus or fair, a group of ethnic travelers, or simply a band of hippies who wander around and never set down roots. It's important that a Ravnos concept fits into this community, acting as a parasite in some cases, a guardian in others (and in many cases they play a role much like a symbiote). Many within these groups are aware that the Ravnos isn't human, even if they don't know exactly what a Vampire is or how they work. This is their cardinal sin against the Camarilla's order; the &quot;trailer trash&quot; who tag around with them all over the continent aren't even ghouled, and they know far too much.<br /> <br /> Side-Bar: The Fall of Animalism<br /> <br /> It is said that Ravana was known as the Tiger Queen, and she rivaled Ennoia in her mastery of Animalism. Many Ravnos Elders and Methuselahs practice the art of Animalism, and it seems that there was a time where the Discipline was much more common within the Clan. The decline in the presence of Animalism seems to have coincided with the fall in the importance of animals in traveling communities; where a traveling band of merchants once had twelve horses, they know have a van and a motorbike. Roma and irish Travelers once kept livestock with them, now at most they have pets.<br /> <br /> A Ravnos may take Animalism as an in-clan Discipline, replacing either Presence or Fortitude, if they wish. They may also take the Additional Discipline merit for Animalism, with a relativley simple justification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T11:01:00-07:00","id":1256756,"title":"","content":"Feedback from my players:<br /> <br /> - Gives them a better reason to be Independent, nice to see that they have divergent values from the other sects rather than just being &quot;thieves and criminals lol&quot;. They're in a position where it makes sense for them to be independent, on both sides. The Camarilla don't want them and they don't want the Camarilla, both with good reason.<br /> <br /> - Great revision of the existing lore and concepts<br /> <br /> - They're my favourite clan to play but most STs won't let me play as one, so seeing them made more accessible is really nice<br /> <br /> - You should leave an option for them to have Animalism (Done)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T09:04:02-07:00","id":1513403,"title":"","content":"I want to thank whoever liked some of the posts here and reminded me that I wrote this years ago - despite having written this Ravnos writeup a long time ago I'm very proud of it, and I think it holds up quite well! Since I wrote this I've played Ravnos a few times, and despite not remembering writing this I've tended to play up the idea of them existing outside of the Traditions and the usual norms of Vampire society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T20:38:59-07:00","id":1513499,"title":"","content":"Quite cool ideas!<br /> <br /> I must have missed this thread when it first appeared.<br /> <br /> In my games I run the Ravnos as generally being composed of &quot;criminals and knights&quot; They tend to recruit from and spend time with criminal groups, but they also target them or those who go too far. They're &quot;knights&quot; in the sense that they protect the bottom rungs of society from other criminals or the corrupt government. They sort of play into the positive (and largely imaginary) stereotypes of groups like the Yakuza or the Mafia as criminal organizations that try to protect the people. So the Ravnos are demons who hunt other demons that prey on the weak and those at the bottom rungs of society.<br /> <br /> This leads from their Clan flaw, which in my games takes the form of both a virtue and a vice that the Ravnos feels compelled to follow. They're very much a paradoxical clan who are both saint and sinner. Of course, individual members may be more or less inclined towards being more saintly or sinful, and many of them are more than happy to indulge in their vices, but even those who are quite evil, have shed their Humanity and are on Paths still feel compelled to give back and help those who are less fortunate.<br /> <br /> I basically got rid of the &quot;traveler&quot; component from the Ravnos, because the Gangrel already do that and that component was largely there as an excuse to tie the Ravnos to the Roma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-31-2023, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T00:11:28-07:00","id":1513505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1513499#post1513499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I basically got rid of the &quot;traveler&quot; component from the Ravnos, because the Gangrel already do that and that component was largely there as an excuse to tie the Ravnos to the Roma.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the &quot;traveler&quot; component is also there to make the Ravnos foils for the Gangrel. Having two clans compete for the same resources prevents the Gangrel from fucking off forever from normal Kindred society and eking out an existence without competition. (The Lupines are another problem for nomadic vampires, but I run the Gangrel as having a &quot;special relationship&quot; with the werewolves... and the Ravnos stick to human groups even when traveling.)<br /> <br /> Just something to think about. I get the impulse to make a clean break with the crass ethnic associations of the Ravnos, though.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 06-01-2023, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T14:27:12-07:00","id":1513710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1513505#post1513505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the &quot;traveler&quot; component is also there to make the Ravnos foils for the Gangrel. Having two clans compete for the same resources prevents the Gangrel from fucking off forever from normal Kindred society and eking out an existence without competition. (The Lupines are another problem for nomadic vampires, but I run the Gangrel as having a &quot;special relationship&quot; with the werewolves... and the Ravnos stick to human groups even when traveling.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I handle things much the same way. The Ravnos exist - as a metagame concept - to cause competition and rivalry for the Gangrel outside the cities. So much of the clan's backstory is &quot;your enemy are the Gangrel&quot;. So the clan needs a reason why characters are outside the city and potentially interacting with the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> I think the distinction between &quot;Gangrel are hardy survivors in the wilderness&quot; and therefore are able to handle Lupines (through various means), and &quot;Ravnos surround themselves with humans which they exploit and then leave before it is too late&quot; is good too. One is physically oriented, the other is socially oriented. One is generally known as straightforward and honorable, the other as deceptive and untrustworthy. Very different approaches despite the general idea that both groups move around a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256534-the-ravnos-paradoxical-rogues?p=1513505#post1513505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just something to think about. I get the impulse to make a clean break with the crass ethnic associations of the Ravnos, though.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The early game definitely overused gypsies. Gypsies were an obvious trope for the generic \u00dcberwald-type gothic horror stories of the past, They are found in the traditional horror literature and early horror movies, and they were definitely a strong influence on the game. So referencing it in some way makes sense. But using them so much treated the group much less like real people than if they were just a fictional concept. So the reaction against them was justifiable.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, going the whole &quot;Indian vampires&quot; route didn't fix the root issue, it just transferred it to a different/larger ethnicity.<br /> <br /> I think a better solution would have been to just move beyond any specific ethnic group and stay with the nomadic exploiters archetype. There were always plenty of people who made their living by travelling a lot - transhumance pastoralists; merchants/salespeople; sailors; religious pilgrims; occupations on long haul trucks, trains, and airliners; highwaymen; migrant smugglers; livestock drovers; natural resource developers that exploit a natural resource and quickly move on; circus/carnival performers; perpetual vacationers/RVers; etc. Then the Roma just becomes one way this can be done, but there's plenty of others who can fit the same niche even in many different human cultures and historical eras.<br /> <br /> The only challenge is to explain why it is in the culture of the clan to always keep moving, and how long do Ravnos typically stay in an area before leaving. The idea of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> description that the clan has a culture of not respecting any of the traditions is something that definitely helps justify it. You just need to develop some detailed lore - probably involving the Ravnos antedeluvian and how Caine and the other antedeluvians treated him - to explain why that culture developed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}